<div class="page-header">
  <div class="kicker">Product Strategy Intelligence Report &bull; Q1 2026</div>
  <h1>Generative AI Competitive Landscape:<br>User Sentiment &amp; Complaint Analysis Across Top 5 AI Apps</h1>
  <div class="meta">
    <span>📊 50,000 reviews analyzed (41,729 after quality filter)</span>
    <span>📅 Dataset: May 2025 – March 2026</span>
    <span>📱 Source: US Google Play Store</span>
    <span>🔬 Apps: ChatGPT · Copilot · Gemini · Perplexity · Claude</span>
  </div>
</div>

<main>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW                                  -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section" id="executive-overview">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">01</span>
    <h2>Executive Overview</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="exec-grid">
    <div class="exec-card c1">
      <div class="num">Microsoft Copilot</div>
      <div class="label">Clear Satisfaction Leader</div>
      <p>Highest average star rating (4.24★) and sentiment polarity (+0.49), with the lowest total complaint rate (9.7%). Copilot's reviews also show the least sentiment-rating divergence (8.1%), signaling authentic, coherent user satisfaction — not noise.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="exec-card c2">
      <div class="num">Claude &amp; Perplexity</div>
      <div class="label">Pricing Friction Risk</div>
      <p>Both apps carry the highest pricing complaint rates in the dataset — Claude at 8.0% and Perplexity at 7.5%. Perplexity pricing reviews average only 1.98★, the harshest complaint category across all five apps. This is a retention-threatening signal.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="exec-card c3">
      <div class="num">Bug Complaints = Viral Risk</div>
      <div class="label">Bugs Earn the Most Upvotes</div>
      <p>Bug/Performance reviews receive an average of 6.9 upvotes vs 1.6 for general reviews — 4× amplification. Claude (5.5%) and Google Gemini (5.2%) have the highest bug complaint rates, meaning their performance issues reach the widest audiences.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight">
    <strong>Dataset Scope &amp; Coverage Caveat</strong>
    Analysis covers 41,729 quality-filtered reviews from the US Google Play Store. Coverage is uneven across apps — ChatGPT and Google Gemini data spans only ~1 month (March 2026 and late Feb–March 2026 respectively), while Claude and Microsoft Copilot data spans nearly a full year (May 2025–March 2026). Temporal comparisons should be interpreted with this imbalance in mind. All percentage KPIs are computed within each app's available review pool.
  </div>

  <div class="chart-card" style="margin-top:24px;">
    <div class="chart-title">At-a-Glance: Key Metrics Across All 5 Apps</div>
    <div class="legend-row">
      <div class="legend-item"><span style="width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--chatgpt);display:inline-block;"></span>ChatGPT</div>
      <div class="legend-item"><span style="width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--copilot);display:inline-block;"></span>Microsoft Copilot</div>
      <div class="legend-item"><span style="width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--gemini);display:inline-block;"></span>Google Gemini</div>
      <div class="legend-item"><span style="width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--perplexity);display:inline-block;"></span>Perplexity</div>
      <div class="legend-item"><span style="width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--claude);display:inline-block;"></span>Claude</div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:300px;">
      <canvas id="radarChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- SECTION 2: CROSS-APP SENTIMENT COMPARISON                      -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section" id="app-sentiment-comparison">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">02</span>
    <h2>Cross-App Sentiment Comparison</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="kpi-strip">
    <div class="kpi-box">
      <div><span class="app-dot" style="background:var(--copilot)"></span></div>
      <div class="kpi-val" style="color:var(--copilot)">4.24★</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Microsoft Copilot</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Sentiment +0.487</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-box">
      <div><span class="app-dot" style="background:var(--chatgpt)"></span></div>
      <div class="kpi-val" style="color:var(--chatgpt)">3.81★</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">ChatGPT</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Sentiment +0.370</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-box">
      <div><span class="app-dot" style="background:var(--claude)"></span></div>
      <div class="kpi-val" style="color:var(--claude)">3.79★</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Claude</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Sentiment +0.375</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-box">
      <div><span class="app-dot" style="background:var(--gemini)"></span></div>
      <div class="kpi-val" style="color:var(--gemini)">3.51★</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Google Gemini</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Sentiment +0.294</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-box">
      <div><span class="app-dot" style="background:var(--perplexity)"></span></div>
      <div class="kpi-val" style="color:var(--perplexity)">3.45★</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Perplexity</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Sentiment +0.313</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <div class="chart-title">Average Star Rating by App</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:260px;">
        <canvas id="avgStarChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <div class="chart-title">Mean VADER Sentiment Polarity by App</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:260px;">
        <canvas id="sentimentChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-card wide">
    <div class="chart-title">Star Rating Distribution (% of reviews per star tier)</div>
    <div class="chart-wrap" style="height:280px;">
      <canvas id="ratingDistChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight">
    <strong>Bimodal Polarization</strong>
    Every app shows a bimodal distribution — heavy concentrations at 1-star and 5-star with thin middle ground. This signals a segmented user base: enthusiastic adopters and frustrated churners, with few neutral experiences. Perplexity has the highest 1-star share (31.3%) despite also having a large 5-star contingent, suggesting the sharpest divide between its user cohorts.
  </div>

  <div class="dq-note">
    <strong>Data Quality Note — Zero Polarity Reviews:</strong> 7.6%–14.6% of reviews per app have a VADER sentiment score of exactly 0.0, caused by Unicode-styled text (bold/italic characters) that the VADER model cannot parse. Google Gemini is most affected (14.6%). These reviews are included in averages as-is; actual mean polarity scores may be slightly higher than reported if these were scored accurately.
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- SECTION 3: THEMATIC COMPLAINT ANALYSIS                         -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
